cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MedicaidGuard-XAI: an explainable, statistically validated framework for prioritising suspicious Medicaid billing and EVV activity"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hossain
    given-names: Md Sibbir
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0795-4512"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sibbirhossain/medicaidguard-xai"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
keywords:
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - healthcare program integrity
  - anomaly detection
  - electronic visit verification
  - Medicaid
abstract: >
  A research prototype that combines transparent rules, supervised learning,
  unsupervised anomaly detection and hybrid risk fusion to prioritise
  suspicious Medicaid personal-care billing and Electronic Visit Verification
  activity for human review. All results are produced on synthetic data with
  simulated labels; the system makes no eligibility or payment decision and
  produces review recommendations rather than findings of fraud.
